  "body": "## What changed\n\n\"Do not touch\" now applies to 2D Adaptive operations, with the Spiral method and with the Trochoidal method. Before this change, the operation refused the protected items.\n\n- `do_not_touch_applies` accepts `OpType::Adaptive2D`. The refusal text, the MCP tool description and the guide name 2D Adaptive with Trace (#3348), 2D Offset, 3D Pocket and Face (#3343).\n- The new module `machining2d::adaptive_avoid` gives one law to the two methods:\n  - The keep-out is one region. It covers each tip height from the floor up to the clearance plane. Thus it holds every cut, every entry and every descent of the path, for the flutes, the shank and the holder.\n  - The planner removes that region from its cutter-centre area. Then it plans as it does without protection. The crossing law, the entry and link certificates and the Offset-rings fallback (Spiral) or the move check (Trochoidal) read the reduced area.\n  - Rapid links are lifted over the items (`elevate_rapid_links`). A link that cannot clear them refuses the operation.\n  - A corner relief that enters the keep-out refuses the operation, as on 2D Offset.\n  - When no item reaches the region, both methods call the plain planner. The path does not change.\n- **Pass starts at** (#3355) is read on the protected Spiral path too (`adaptive_spiral_avoid_on`). The Trochoidal method still refuses Inside and Outside by name.\n- The generic checks in `generate.rs` (`route_links`, `verify_avoid`) and the post gate (`live_avoid_problems`) already read each kind that `do_not_touch_applies` accepts. They have no change.\n\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/3346-adaptive2d-do-not-touch.md` (with the dropped options).\n\n**Known cost:** 2D Adaptive plans one area for all levels. Beside a protected item that is lower than the top of the cut, it leaves more stock than 2D Offset, which keeps out level by level. The guide says so. This costs cut area. It does not cost safety.\n\n## Merge of main\n\nThe branch merges `upstream/main` three times:\n\n- `1d1bd090f` (main `6cfc0a6d4`): conflicts with #3343 (Face) in `do_not_touch_applies`, its refusal text, the MCP description, the UI test and the guide. Both sides are kept. A conflict with #3355 in the 2D Adaptive arm of `generate.rs` is resolved by commit `067a914a1`, which threads the `StartSide` into the protected Spiral path.\n- `f73493967` (main `74ea8988d`): no conflict.\n- `241f6aeb5` (main `f35202134`): conflicts with #3348 (Trace) in `do_not_touch_applies`, its refusal text, the MCP description and the UI test. Both sides are kept: the list is now \"Trace, 2D Offset, 2D Adaptive, 3D Pocket and Face\". Main also removed \"only so far\" from the refusal text. Thus the 2D Adaptive UI test now checks that no \"is supported on\" note shows. The old check looked for text that main no longer writes.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- motion `avoid_adaptive`:\n  - `a_spiral_adaptive_keeps_the_full_tool_clear_of_a_protected_pin_with_no_crossing`\n  - `a_spiral_adaptive_with_no_keepout_on_the_region_is_the_plain_path`\n  - `a_spiral_adaptive_with_a_pass_start_keeps_the_full_tool_clear_of_a_protected_pin`\n  - `a_trochoidal_adaptive_keeps_the_full_tool_clear_of_a_protected_pin`\n  - `an_empty_avoid_gives_the_plain_trochoidal_path`\n  - `a_trochoidal_adaptive_with_no_room_left_is_refused_with_the_item_named`\n- app `do_not_touch_adaptive`:\n  - `adaptive2d_do_not_touch_keeps_the_full_tool_clear_and_clears_back_to_the_plain_path`\n  - `adaptive2d_with_no_room_clear_of_the_protection_is_refused_with_the_item_named`\n  - `adaptive2d_do_not_touch_round_the_tower_at_the_default_load_posts` (heavy lane)\n- ui `do_not_touch`:\n  - `adaptive2d_shows_the_pick_protected_button_and_no_unsupported_note`\n  - `unsupported_op_shows_do_not_touch_note_without_pick_button` (new text)\n\n## Gates\n\nOn `241f6aeb5` (the head of this PR):\n\n- Quick gate (`CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1 cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): 769 steps, 0 failed, 1 stalled. The stalled step is `ui suites: lib`: it gave no output for 15 min. The cause is local: on the author's machine the NVIDIA Vulkan driver hangs in `vkEnumerateInstanceExtensionProperties` while it waits for an X server reply (`vulkaninfo` hangs too). Each GPU lib test hangs there, and the #3589 lock holds the other GPU tests behind it. A rerun of that step alone with `DISPLAY` unset (`--only \"ui suites: lib\"`) passed: 1493 tests, 91 s.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`): 253 steps, 0 failed, 56.6 min. Four known fails were red as expected (#1950 three times, #2849 one time).\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. Without `--no-deps`, clippy stops in `camcraft-gpu` (`needless_range_loop`). This branch does not change that crate, and main has the same code.\n\nEarlier runs:\n\n- On `f73493967`: quick gate 765 steps, 0 failed (one stall in `app build (--no-run)`, which passed alone). Heavy lanes 252 steps, 0 failed.\n- On `067a914a1`: one failure, `first_part_programs::first_router_part_posts_the_shipped_program`. Main's #3464 left `examples/first-router-part.nc` stale, and main fixed it in `74a87c662`. The merge `f73493967` brings that fix.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No machine air cut.\n- No per-level keep-out. A level above a low protected item loses the same area as the floor level.\n\nChangelog: 2D Adaptive (Spiral and Trochoidal) honours \"Do not touch\": the full tool (flutes, shank, holder) stays clear of each protected face or edge by the clearance, or the operation is refused with the item named.\n\nFixes #3346\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
